  "description": "Executable evidence for ak.vector.keypackage.recipient_claim_read.v1 (zh/crypto-media/device-lifecycle.md section 9 claims/query and section 9.2.4, zh/crypto-media/encryption-and-audit.md section 2.6.1, decision 0119). The Station is the claim destination; alice, on the same Station, claimed bob_claim for bob_device and agent_claim for the Agent's current runtime key, and the Station stored each claim request's outcome, with a claim_receipt signed by its own service key, before answering alice. A read variant has reader call ak.self.keys.keypackages.read.claim.v1 for claim at clock (inside retention unless after_retention) and compares the answer with the stored bytes; state_writes counts writes the read made and claim_state and keypackage_state are read afterwards. A receive variant has bob_device read bob_claim and run the recipient checks in order: the read itself, the claims_digest recomputation, the receipt signature under the Station's service key, then the binding of claim, Welcome, winning Add Commit and current endpoint authorization; refused_by names the first check that refuses, and only an accepted variant may join the group from the Welcome.",
